Improper Authentication and Data Handling The application handles user credentials and authentication, which can lead to vulnerabilities if not properly managed, such as weak password storage or improper session management., SQL Injection and Data Exposure User inputs are directly used in database queries, which can lead to SQL injection if not properly sanitized, potentially exposing sensitive user data.

